  "body": "Follow-up from NeoTech's review of #1101 (#931 slice 1). `grblhal.cps` (~302) and `tinyg.cps` (~298) don't declare `workOffsetIndex`; they read `PARAM WorkOffset` as the word and put it into the header. With #1101's engine they run on the unflagged path: offsets 1-6 post exactly G54..G59, and offset 7 or higher is refused by setup name. So nothing is posted wrong; the gap is only consistency.\n\n**Done means:** both scripts declare `workOffsetIndex = true` and `workOffsetMax = 6` (G54-G59 per their public docs) and write their own word from the 1-based number. They are added to the script list in `work_offset_index.rs`, the `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` exception sentence is removed, and their goldens are byte-identical.\n",
